WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.900
"Does Aluminum Cause Alzheimer's Disease?"

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.480
The so-called
"aluminum hypothesis"

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.280
for the cause
of Alzheimer's disease

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.100
dates back to 1965,

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.620
when the inadvertent
injection of aluminum

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.000
into the brains of rabbits

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.980
caused neurological symptoms

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.580
along with what initially
looked like Alzheimer's disease

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.320
tangles in the brain.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.380
Then, in the 1970s,
it was first reported

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.420
that the aluminum content
of Alzheimer's brains

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.720
was higher than that
of control brains on autopsy.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.140
Following that, there was
a rash of fatal dementia cases

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.060
attributed to dialysis fluids

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.500
contaminated with aluminum.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.600
This trio of findings

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.120
led researchers
to suggest that aluminum,

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.340
the third most
abundant element on Earth

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.720
(after oxygen and silicon),

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.300
may play a role
in the development

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.860
of Alzheimer's disease.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.680
The first crack in the theory

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.200
was the realization that,
upon closer inspection,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.300
the tangle-like changes
in rabbit brains

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.220
were not much like those

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.800
found in human
Alzheimer's disease after all.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.880
The changes in aluminum-induced
dialysis encephalopathy

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.620
were also dissimilar.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.560
Aluminum could certainly
be toxic to the brain,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.940
but not necessarily in a way

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.100
that had anything to do
with Alzheimer's disease.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.160
And, subsequent autopsy studies
of Alzheimer's victims

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.160
did not consistently find
higher aluminum levels,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.280
and even if they did,
elevations in brain aluminum

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.440
could be a consequence
rather than a cause

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.840
(reflecting
Alzheimer's disease damage

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.160
to the blood brain barrier).

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.100
The aluminum hypothesis
came under heavy fire

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.420
in the scientific community.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.480
Only later did we learn
that the most vocal critics

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.300
were secretly-paid
aluminum industry hacks.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.740
In hindsight,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.820
that was probably unnecessary,

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.940
as the tide of evidence
eventually turned against

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.200
the role of aluminum.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.820
What convinced me

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.760
was a meta-analysis
that failed to find a connection

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.940
between regular antacid use
and Alzheimer's.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.520
Processed foods
contain a variety

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.200
of aluminum-containing
additives,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.900
such as anti-caking agents
in pancake mix,

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.760
melting agents
in American cheese,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.380
meat binders, gravy thickeners,

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.420
rising agents
in some baking powders,

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.100
and dye binders in candy.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.340
However,
over-the-counter antacids

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.800
are probably
the most important source

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.380
for human aluminum exposure
in terms of dose.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.560
In terms of the safety
of dietary aluminum,

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.600
the tolerable weekly intake

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.060
is 1 mg per healthy kilogram
of body weight.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.820
So, if you weigh
about 150 pounds (67.5 kg),

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.820
you shouldn't get more than,
like, 10 milligrams a day.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.280
One day of Maalox

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.160
can give you
38 hundred milligrams,

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.680
nearly 400 times
the daily safety limit,

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.140
and nowhere on the label
does it say

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.240
not to take
with acidic beverages,

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.260
such as fruit juice.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.900
Washing an antacid down
with orange juice

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.540
can increase
aluminum absorption eight-fold.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.700
The total aluminum intake

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.380
in drinking water
and processed foods

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.960
in most countries may only
be a few milligrams a day.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.440
But, some antacids can increase
daily aluminum consumption

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.120
by up to several grams,

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.860
a thousand-fold higher.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.800
And so, if antacid use

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.900
isn't related
to Alzheimer's risk,

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.340
then ingested aluminum

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.260
is unlikely to be a cause.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.580
Now, as I explored
in my video on cooking with it,

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.860
just because aluminum
doesn't cause Alzheimer's

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.860
doesn't mean aluminum intake
is necessarily benign.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:24.600
Those who cook with aluminum

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.280
and store acidic foods,

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.260
like yogurt and tomato,
in aluminum cookware

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:31.560
suffer significantly more
DNA damage,

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.020
leading some regulators
to recommend consumers

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.360
avoid the use
of aluminum pots or dishes

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.580
for acidic or salted foodstuffs.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:41.580
In my video on antiperspirants
and breast cancer,

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.880
I note how the FDA
and European safety authorities

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.620
specifically advise against

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.860
using aluminum antiperspirants
on damaged skin,

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:52.920
which may even include
avoiding them after shaving.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.440
As a "metalloestrogen,"

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.540
aluminum absorption may explain

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.900
why breast cancer may occur
as much as twenty years earlier

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.900
in women using antiperspirant
and shaving their armpits

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.220
more than three times a week.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.940
You can also avoid
high dietary sources

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.700
by choosing non-aluminum
baking powder for baking

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.800
and avoiding
processed cheese.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.900
Aluminum salts can give cheese
"desirable slicing properties,"

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.360
but that means a single
grilled cheese sandwich

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.880
can end up exceeding
the World Health Organization's

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.340
provisional tolerable
daily intake of aluminum

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.020
by as much as 400 percent.

